WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
What is a day trade?. Opening and closing a position during the same trading day.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
A same-day example. Buy at 10 a.m. Monday. Sell at 2 p.m. Monday. That is a day trade.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
A different-day example. Buy on Monday and sell on Friday. This is not a same-day trade.

4
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Speed brings risk. Fast price movements can create losses quickly. Frequent trades do not guarantee income.

5
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Learn before you trade. Sprout runs simulated prices 24/7. Real US regular sessions generally run 9:30 a.m.–4 p.m. Eastern on trading days.

